@startuml Google OAuth 2.0 Server-Side Token Validation Flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam maxmessagesize 60

title Google OAuth 2.0 Server-Side Token Validation Flow\nCurrent Implementation - Verified Working

actor User as U
participant "Frontend\n(App.tsx)" as FE
participant "WalletModal\n(.tsx)" as WM
participant "Google OAuth\nLibrary" as GLIB
participant "Google Platform\n(OAuth)" as GOOGLE
participant "Backend\n(Controller)" as BE
participant "Google Auth\nService" as SVC

== OAuth Initiation ==
U -> FE: Access ngrok URL\nhttps://b0280d99b435.ngrok-free.app
activate FE
U -> FE: Click "Connect Wallet"
FE -> WM: Show WalletModal
activate WM
U -> WM: Click "Connect with Google"

WM -> WM: handleConnect('google')\ncalls googleLogin()
WM -> GLIB: useGoogleLogin.onSuccess
activate GLIB

note over GLIB: @react-oauth/google library\nhandles popup/redirect flow

GLIB -> GOOGLE: OAuth 2.0 Authorization Request\n(popup or redirect)
activate GOOGLE
GOOGLE -> U: Show Google login screen\n(if not already logged in)
U -> GOOGLE: Enter Google credentials
GOOGLE -> U: Show consent screen\n(email, profile permissions)
U -> GOOGLE: Accept permissions

GOOGLE -> GLIB: Return access_token\n+ expires_in + token_type
deactivate GOOGLE
GLIB -> WM: onSuccess(response)\nresponse.access_token
deactivate GLIB

== Backend Token Validation ==
WM -> WM: setConnectionState('connecting')

WM -> BE: POST /auth/google/validate\nContent-Type: application/json\nbody: { access_token: "ya29.a0..." }\nheader: ngrok-skip-browser-warning
activate BE

BE -> BE: validateToken()\nExtract access_token from body

BE -> SVC: validateGoogleToken(access_token)
activate SVC

SVC -> GOOGLE: GET /tokeninfo?access_token=TOKEN\nValidate token with Google
activate GOOGLE
GOOGLE -> SVC: Token info response:\n{ aud, exp, email, sub, ... }
deactivate GOOGLE

SVC -> SVC: Verify token audience\n(aud === GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID)
alt Invalid audience
    SVC -> BE: throw Error("Token not for this app")
    BE -> WM: HTTP 400: Token validation failed
end

SVC -> SVC: Check token expiration\n(exp > current_time)
alt Token expired
    SVC -> BE: throw Error("Token has expired")
    BE -> WM: HTTP 400: Token expired
end

SVC -> GOOGLE: GET /oauth2/v3/userinfo\nAuthorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN
activate GOOGLE
GOOGLE -> SVC: User profile:\n{ sub, email, name, picture, email_verified, ... }
deactivate GOOGLE

SVC -> SVC: Create JWT token:\n{ provider: 'google',\n  googleId: sub,\n  email: email,\n  name: name,\n  picture: picture,\n  emailVerified: email_verified,\n  verified: email_verified,\n  authenticatedAt: timestamp }\nSign with JWT_SECRET (1h expiration)

SVC -> BE: { jwtToken, userData }
deactivate SVC

BE -> WM: HTTP 200:\n{ success: true,\n  auth_token: JWT_TOKEN,\n  user_data: { ... } }
deactivate BE

== Frontend Token Processing ==
WM -> WM: Create googleAuth object:\n{ provider: 'google',\n  googleId: user_data.googleId,\n  email: user_data.email,\n  name: user_data.name,\n  picture: user_data.picture,\n  verified: user_data.verified,\n  token: auth_token }

WM -> WM: setConnectionState('connected')

WM -> FE: onAuthSuccess(googleAuth)
WM -> FE: Modal closes
deactivate WM

FE -> FE: handleAuthSuccess(googleAuth)\nsetUser(googleAuth)\nsetShowWalletModal(false)

FE -> U: Show "Connected" status\nDisplay: "Connected: google (user@...)"
deactivate FE

== Success State ==
note over U, FE: User is now authenticated with Google\nJWT token stored in frontend state\nNo sensitive tokens persisted\nServer-side validation completed

== Alternative Error Flows ==
note over SVC, BE: Error scenarios:\n• Invalid access token → HTTP 400\n• Wrong audience → HTTP 400\n• Expired token → HTTP 400\n• Network failure → HTTP 500\n• Missing client ID → HTTP 400

@enduml